        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                "word": "sacrificateur",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e502fb93-0c88-4e7a-aa63-6ed0f1f736e7",
                        "entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sacrificateurs"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d577e8c4-d55e-49be-ab99-7a5c7b6da1b1",
                        "entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "sacrificatrice"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                        "entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celui qui sacrifie, ministre préposé pour faire les sacrifices, en parlant des religions qui pratiquent des sacrifices."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b55cbce-fd6d-4220-8e23-613fed025d51",
                                "sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                                "text": "Les sacrificateurs s’emparèrent de la victime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9353bfc7-590e-4190-8892-5e02e7bc7a47",
                                "sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                                "text": "Pendant les derniers moments de mon séjour à Vendôme, Louis ne sentait plus l’aiguillon de la gloire, il avait, en quelque sorte, abstractivement joui de la renommée ; et après l’avoir ouverte, comme les anciens sacrificateurs qui cherchaient l’avenir au cœur des hommes, il n’avait rien trouvé dans les entrailles de cette Chimère."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6b9260d-54df-46bf-b658-8524d81c2ec7",
                                "sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                                "text": "« Saint-Loup au casque d'airain, dit Bloch, reprenez un peu de ce canard aux cuisses lourdes de graisse sur lesquelles l'illustre sacrificateur des volailles a répandu de nombreuses libations de vin rouge. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa754bdd-d44a-435d-a61b-567de532f749",
                                "sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                                "text": "L’idée s’impose en effet qu’en échange de la nourriture qui leur est offerte, les dieux, les esprits ou les ancêtres adressent leur « avis » aux sacrificateurs, à condition que des règles soient respectées, en particulier en ce qui concerne la nature de l’offrande et le moment où elle intervient."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5bb60ea7-760b-4767-9397-f55e45c292cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "source_sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                        "target_lang_word": "Priester",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Priester",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ae542ea-c065-3622-b19a-d686fd5ccb1b",
                                        "entry_id": "1e62bcd2-281b-313d-bc6b-6dc9ac2eb7e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mittler zwischen dem menschlichen und göttlichen Bereich, zum Beispiel durch Opfer"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Religionsgeschichte"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9fa4c0a-0905-475f-8a67-cb7de33e3f3c",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae542ea-c065-3622-b19a-d686fd5ccb1b",
                                                "text": "Die ägyptischen Priester waren hoch angesehen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b1ee45e-a616-4924-982b-fe3b86dd7a5f",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae542ea-c065-3622-b19a-d686fd5ccb1b",
                                                "text": "„Der Priester als Mittler zwischen Mensch und göttlicher Welt findet sich auch heute noch bei Kulturen mit Ackerbau und Viehzucht (zu denen die Kelten gehörten), während der Schamane bei den Jägern, Sammlern und Hirtennomaden anzutreffen ist.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29cd2fc9-6310-4ee0-bbb6-5d1ebddb283c",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae542ea-c065-3622-b19a-d686fd5ccb1b",
                                                "text": "„Die dargestellten Personen tragen eindeutig keltische Kleidung, eine Szene stellt wahrscheinlich Opferhandlungen mit einem Priester dar.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9da5938e-8d58-45ac-9aec-46c08eb8102f",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae542ea-c065-3622-b19a-d686fd5ccb1b",
                                                "text": "„Der Arzt sieht den Menschen in seiner ganzen Schwäche, der Advokat in seiner ganzen Schlechtigkeit und der Priester in seiner ganzen Dummheit.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                        "entry_id": "1e62bcd2-281b-313d-bc6b-6dc9ac2eb7e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Amtsträger in der Kirche, dauerhaft bestellt durch die Priesterweihe"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a790eef-7bb1-4188-b558-295025b24b41",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "„Der Arzt sieht den Menschen in seiner ganzen Schwäche, der Advokat in seiner ganzen Schlechtigkeit und der Priester in seiner ganzen Dummheit.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f29b311-b083-415a-a232-332dc59539fd",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "Als Priester kann man Pfarrer werden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caf4068c-9094-470c-a480-a4033c75793f",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "„Es nützte nichts, weder der Priester noch sonst jemand vermochte ihn davon abzubringen, daß ich nicht sein Diener, sondern sein Sklave sei…“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b44e075a-fcd0-47e1-958e-4229cbc99e19",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "„Der Priester ist nicht gekommen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "344e5cb2-63e4-4c0c-8231-ffec84eeda5f",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "„Dieser Mann konnte nicht schreiben; aber er schämte sich dessen nicht, denn mit Ausnahme des Priesters und eines Wundarztes besaß niemand im Regiment diese Fertigkeit.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bea9c30-d48d-40b8-bd8d-b807a478ce55",
                                                "sense_id": "12430f78-678a-30f2-b2bd-6539233d5bda",
                                                "text": "„Mochten Adam, Eva (»Heua« bei Luther), Noah und ihr Schöpfer Deutsch gesprochen haben oder nicht, die Priester an den Altären, die Gelehrten auf den Kathedern und die Studenten am Biertisch sprachen Latein.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5f1b3138-eacb-410e-bdd1-939b109bfe43",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "source_sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                        "target_lang_word": "sacrificer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sacrificer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d0fa73a-5a62-306c-820a-6f9ed161d9e6",
                                        "entry_id": "7cfc7141-6e6e-31bf-9524-7d1570753d09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who sacrifices, one who makes a sacrifice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06c69865-51f4-42f9-83e8-2d1cc76ba0e2",
                                                "sense_id": "7d0fa73a-5a62-306c-820a-6f9ed161d9e6",
                                                "text": "Our course will seem too bloody, Caius Cassius,\nTo cut the head off and then hack the limbs,\nLike wrath in death and envy afterwards;\nFor Antony is but a limb of Caesar:\nLet us be sacrificers, but not butchers, Caius."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "181e2e5e-fa8d-4f65-ac75-99ffa12c9d4b",
                                                "sense_id": "7d0fa73a-5a62-306c-820a-6f9ed161d9e6",
                                                "text": "In this you’have made the Court the Antipodes,\nAnd will’d your Delegate, the vulgar Sunne,\nTo doe profane autumnall offices,\nWhilst here to you, wee sacrificers runne;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a231ce0a-3ec1-457f-8f74-eb3c2d95d4e2",
                                                "sense_id": "7d0fa73a-5a62-306c-820a-6f9ed161d9e6",
                                                "text": "So, when some brawny Sacrificer knocks,\nBefore an Altar led, an offer’d Ox,\nHis Eye-balls rooted out, are thrown to Ground;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d6d6bde-06d2-4fe6-a543-032e115a3757",
                                                "sense_id": "7d0fa73a-5a62-306c-820a-6f9ed161d9e6",
                                                "text": "[…] no sacrifice is valid unless the sacrificer lay his hand upon the head of the victim."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13c9162a-e1a1-4ddf-9f16-ebc944c5a9c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4e54b3c-46b5-3746-ad43-5d77037fbd59",
                        "source_sense_id": "53f7d1cc-d92f-322e-9c31-8b18f1e97780",
                        "target_lang_word": "priest",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "priest",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efce5a83-a303-3068-98d2-2d80f713cf5c",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c44922-8cb0-384e-9064-cdd173d1c253",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A religious clergyman (clergywoman, clergyperson) who is trained to perform services or sacrifices at a church or temple."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93341e8a-44f3-4f95-b7cc-a1d10280d18d",
                                                "sense_id": "efce5a83-a303-3068-98d2-2d80f713cf5c",
                                                "text": "The priest at the Catholic church heard his confession."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "669057ab-b4ae-462d-9903-79d834fb901a",
                                                "sense_id": "efce5a83-a303-3068-98d2-2d80f713cf5c",
                                                "text": "The Shinto priest burnt incense for his ancestors."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8b8f450-b8cd-41cd-b982-d4a60ab2d3d9",
                                                "sense_id": "efce5a83-a303-3068-98d2-2d80f713cf5c",
                                                "text": "The Israelite priests were descended from Moses' brother Aaron."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e028db96-9316-4e65-ac3a-f1ead79ee4d4",
                                                "sense_id": "efce5a83-a303-3068-98d2-2d80f713cf5c",
                                                "text": "It was a joy to snatch some brief respite, and find himself in the rectory drawing–room. Listening here was as pleasant as talking; just to watch was pleasant. The young priests who lived here wore cassocks and birettas; their faces were fine and mild, yet really strong, like the rector's face; and in their intercourse with him and his wife they seemed to be brothers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "305009a5-9fb5-3872-8562-1192a993aab2",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c44922-8cb0-384e-9064-cdd173d1c253",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A blunt tool, used for quickly stunning and killing fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3e86ebe-f013-4a4e-922e-48663c4f685e",
                                                "sense_id": "305009a5-9fb5-3872-8562-1192a993aab2",
                                                "text": "They flop and struggle, but she unhooks them swiftly, stunning them with a small brass priest."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4404b956-4504-39d4-a420-912536e15feb",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c44922-8cb0-384e-9064-cdd173d1c253",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The highest office in the Aaronic priesthood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mormonism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "priest",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4a2c7ad-87b7-3157-8c7c-381b1306f840",
                                        "entry_id": "13dda2c7-93fa-3574-99f4-7ce47856907e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To ordain as a priest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6856fbf2-3168-4d39-b963-642e4cd1aa5f",
                                                "sense_id": "d4a2c7ad-87b7-3157-8c7c-381b1306f840",
                                                "text": "If there bee any lasie fellow, any that cannot away with worke, any that would wallow in pleasures, hee is hastie to be priested. And when hee is made one, and has gotten a benefice, he consorts with his neighbour priests, who are altogether given to pleasures; and then both hee, and they, live, not like Christians, but like epicures; drinking, eating, feasting, and revelling, till the cow come home, as the saying is."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
